{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-45632",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The hive starts with $4,000$ and then doubles every week. \n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- After $1$ week, there are $4\\,000\\cdot 2$ bees.\n\n- After $2$ weeks, there are $4\\,000\\cdot {2}^{2}$ bees.\n\n- After $3$ weeks, there are $4\\,000\\cdot {2}^{3}$ bees.\n\nSo the correct expression for the number of bees after $3$ weeks is $4\\,000\\cdot {2}^{3}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
